```java
public class HeapVsStackDemo {
    int instanceField = 42;           // lives on the HEAP (inside the object)

    void process(int param) {         // 'param' + locals live on the STACK
        int local = param + 1;        // stack: a primitive value
        var obj = new HeapVsStackDemo(); // 'obj' ref on stack, object on heap
        System.out.println(local + obj.instanceField);
    } // stack frame popped here; the heap object waits for the GC

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new HeapVsStackDemo().process(10); // prints 53
    }
}
```
The reference `obj` sits on the stack, but the object it points to lives on the shared heap.

